{
  "title": "Drum Rack 32",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "Move's Drum Rack with",
        "32 pads, not 16.",
        "",
        "Loads Move's own kits",
        "and plays them with",
        "the same sampler",
        "voice, so a kit built",
        "on the device sounds",
        "like itself here.",
        "",
        "DR32 opens empty.",
        "Load a kit from the",
        "Category page."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pages",
      "lines": [
        "Jog moves between",
        "pages.",
        "",
        "Category",
        " pick a kit",
        "Pads",
        " sample and tuning",
        "Pads 2",
        " envelope and filter",
        "Pads 3",
        " level, sends, punch",
        "Master",
        " level for the kit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Loading kits",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Category",
          "lines": [
            "Click to go in, then",
            "click a row to open",
            "that group's kits.",
            "",
            "Acoustic, Electronic",
            "and Hybrid come from",
            "Move's own library.",
            "My Kits is what you",
            "have made.",
            "",
            "Only real drum kits",
            "are listed. Your",
            "preset folder holds",
            "presets for every",
            "instrument, and most",
            "cannot load as a",
            "rack."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Scrolling loads",
          "lines": [
            "Moving the cursor",
            "loads the kit under",
            "it, a moment after",
            "you stop. So you can",
            "hear your way",
            "through a group.",
            "",
            "There is NO undo.",
            "The kit you were on",
            "is replaced. Save",
            "first."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pads",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Choosing a pad",
          "lines": [
            "32 pads, notes",
            "36 to 67.",
            "",
            "Hit a pad and the",
            "editor follows it,",
            "while the transport",
            "is stopped.",
            "",
            "The PAD knob picks",
            "a pad by hand,",
            "1 to 32."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Page 1",
          "lines": [
            "PAD   which pad",
            "SMPL  open a",
            " browser in that",
            " pad's own folder",
            "STRT  start point",
            "END   end point",
            "TRSP  semitones",
            "DETN  cents",
            "CHOKE choke group.",
            " Pads sharing one",
            " cut each other off",
            "BRWS  step through",
            " the folder, one",
            " sample per detent"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Page 2",
          "lines": [
            "ATK   attack",
            "DCY   decay",
            "HOLD  hold",
            "ENV   A-H-D or",
            "      A-S-R",
            "CUT   filter freq",
            "RES   resonance",
            "TYPE  filter type,",
            " four of them",
            "FILT  filter on/off"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Page 3",
          "lines": [
            "VVOL  how much",
            " velocity moves",
            " the level",
            "VOL   pad level",
            "PAN   pad position",
            "LINK  see Link",
            "SNDA  send A amount",
            "SNDB  send B amount",
            "PUNCH transient",
            " shaper. Above",
            " zero it turns",
            " itself on",
            "PTIME punch time"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Link",
      "lines": [
        "LINK sets one",
        "control across every",
        "pad.",
        "",
        "Click it on, turn a",
        "knob, and every pad",
        "takes that value.",
        "",
        "It releases as soon",
        "as you touch another",
        "control, so the next",
        "knob is that pad's",
        "alone.",
        "",
        "It never spreads",
        "what makes a pad its",
        "own: the sample, the",
        "note, or the browse",
        "spot.",
        "",
        "It is off whenever",
        "DR32 loads."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sends",
      "lines": [
        "Each pad has its own",
        "SNDA and SNDB",
        "amount, in dB,",
        "feeding the two",
        "global return buses.",
        "",
        "Put an effect on a",
        "return and every pad",
        "can tap it at its",
        "own level. One",
        "reverb for the kit,",
        "not one per pad.",
        "",
        "A kit from Move",
        "brings its own send",
        "amounts.",
        "",
        "Needs host 1.3.0. On",
        "an older host the",
        "knobs still turn and",
        "save, but nothing",
        "reads them.",
        "",
        "DR32 has no effects",
        "of its own."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Saving",
      "lines": [
        "Your edits are",
        "stored in the",
        "Schwung set, on top",
        "of the kit that was",
        "loaded.",
        "",
        "So a set records",
        "which kit you used",
        "and what you",
        "changed.",
        "",
        "Kits are Move's own",
        "files and are never",
        "modified."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Limits",
      "lines": [
        "Pads 17 to 32 are",
        "outside Move's 4x4",
        "pad map, so the",
        "small map in the",
        "header does not",
        "light for them.",
        "",
        "Pad effects besides",
        "Punch are kept when",
        "a kit is saved, so",
        "kits reopen on Move,",
        "but are not played",
        "back.",
        "",
        "Effects saved in a",
        "kit's return chain",
        "are kept, but not",
        "set up for you.",
        "",
        "Browsing kits has no",
        "undo."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
